2. Dependencies linked into the shipped binaries
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

`rop-finder` and `rop-finder-mcp` statically link their whole dependency graph.
The complete, exact set is Cargo.lock, which is tracked in this repository for
exactly this reason; `cargo deny check licenses` in CI is the enforcement point.
The dependencies whose code is most visible in this tool's output are:

  capstone 0.13.0 (crate: MIT) — builds and statically links the Capstone
    disassembly engine's vendored C sources, whose own license reads
    "Copyright (c) 2013, COSEINC. All rights reserved." (BSD 3-clause, plus
    LICENSE_LLVM.TXT for the LLVM-derived portions). Capstone was designed and
    implemented by Nguyen Anh Quynh. https://www.capstone-engine.org
  iced-x86 1.21.0 (MIT) — the x86/x64 instruction formatter.
  goblin 0.10.7 (MIT) — ELF/PE/Mach-O parsing.
  rmcp 3.2.0 (Apache-2.0) — the Model Context Protocol server runtime.

Full per-crate license texts are not vendored here; each ships in the
corresponding crate's own source, which `cargo vendor` will lay out for you if
you need to assemble a complete notice file for a downstream distribution.


